REIMAGINE: Why now: pilot live (#1109), seven real journal entries, first accepted dream report — threshold exercisable against real data. Simplest path: (a) adherence test pinning step 11's negative semantics (no question/waiting/invocation/timer) in the pattern of tests/test_lair_state_via_pr.py; (b) inline counting one-liner in step 11 — journal entry blob ids vs accepted reports' ledgers (DREAM.md v8-r1 requires `<path> blob <40-hex>` per report); (c) one live lair run as validation evidence. No library, no new skill.
ANTIPATTERNS: YAGNI counting script (data exists in report ledgers — inline shell comparison, not scripts/ entry); premature abstraction configurable threshold (hardcode 5); tautological test risk (pin negative semantics, not the string "5").
EXIT-CRITERIA: criterion 1 substantively met by #1097 (counting unvalidated); criteria 2-4 substantively met by #1119. Decision point: close citing #1097+#1119, or deliver the README-reserved live validation delta (test + counting + live run). No scope substitution either way.
